JIRA ID : AIHPBLAS-5015

Stack, in merge order: #12876, #12960, **#13005 (this PR)**, #13013,
#13015, #13021, #13022, #13025, #13031. The diff here is only the
every-solution, every-iteration layer; the base moves down the stack as
those merge.

## Summary

Address-arithmetic bugs tend to live in a few solutions out of hundreds,
and some only show up on some launches. A test that runs the heuristic's
top pick once can miss both kinds. And when a failure does show up,
nobody can reproduce it unless the report says which solution and which
launch failed.

This PR lets a test run every solution the library offers for a problem,
and launch and check each one several times (`fast_check_repeat`). D is
reset to the sentinel and the workspace to zero before every launch, so
each check sees only that launch's work. One summary at the end lists
every failing solution, its kernel and which launches failed.

Stream-K needs a word of care. On gfx942 the library offers Stream-K
solutions only when the process starts with
`TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2`, which no CI lane sets today, so
the Stream-K cases skip there and are for manual runs. On gfx950
Stream-K is the only library, so they always run, and they overlap the
default cases. A self-test corrupts one launch on purpose, to prove the
report points at the right one. Cases that hit open defects are
quarantined in `known_bugs.yaml`; see Defects found below.

**CI time added** (one MI300X / one MI350X, ROCm 10.2, sum of per-test
times): about 1 s / 2 s in pre_checkin (14 / 26 cases), and about 6 min
/ 3 min in nightly (28 / 29 cases). With
`TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2` on MI300X, this PR's Stream-K
cases add about 4.5 min more.

## Motivation

Each address-arithmetic defect on AIHPBLAS-4988 lives in a handful of
the hundreds of shipped solutions: 2 of 244 in ROCM-32046, 39 of 545 in
ROCM-31290, 4 of 679 in ROCM-31258. Some defects are also intermittent.
ROCM-31901 and ROCM-31905 fail only on some launches, and ROCM-31105
needed repeated launches to show up. A test that runs only the
heuristic's top pick, and checks only the first call, misses both kinds.
When a failure does show up, the report also needs to say which solution
and which launch failed, or nobody can reproduce it.

## Technical Details

Only client test code and test data change.

- **Every iteration.** A new argument, `fast_check_repeat`, launches and
checks each solution that many times, one solution at a time. Before
every launch D is refilled with the sentinel, and the workspace is
returned to the zeros of a fresh allocation, so a repeat cannot pass on
partial sums an earlier launch left there (a Stream-K fixup that reads
too early, for example). Zero rather than poison, because kernels may
rely on their flags starting at zero. A failure message names the
solution, its library index and kernel, and the iteration ("iteration 2
of 4").
- **Summary per solution.** `FastCheckSolutionLog` records pass or fail
for each solution and iteration. At the end of the test, one failure
lists every failing solution with its library index, kernel name and
failing iterations. With hundreds of solutions, that list is the triage
starting point.
- **Self-test.** `fast_check_inject` corrupts one element of D after the
launch on the named iteration. The case passes only if that iteration
fails for every solution, its report names the corrupted element, and
every other iteration passes. The corrupted value is the sentinel, so
this exercises the per-iteration sentinel check; the probe-sum path is
covered by the host self-tests in #12876.
- **Stream-K.** A new argument, `requires_streamk`, skips the case with
a message unless the process started with
`TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2`. On gfx950 the case always runs,
because Stream-K is the only library there. TensileLite reads that
variable once per process (`Debug::Instance`), so
`tensile_solution_selection_method` in a YAML case only has an effect if
no earlier test in the process has run a GEMM. A Stream-K case whose
solutions include no Stream-K kernel (TileProcessingStrategy StreamK,
`TPSSK` in the kernel name) also skips with the reason, rather than
passing while testing none.
- **Every solution.** These cases use `algo_method: all`, which already
includes the hand-written custom kernels (ROCM-31258). A new xf32 case
on gfx950 runs them all.

New YAML cases:

- pre_checkin: the self-test (f32 and bf16, 4 solutions × 4 iterations);
the heuristic's first 16 solutions × 4 iterations in f32, f16 and bf16
for every transpose; and the same under Stream-K.
- nightly: every supported solution × 3 iterations in f32, f16 and bf16
on two ragged shapes; xf32 with custom kernels on gfx950; and every
Stream-K solution × 3 iterations.

## Defects found

The cluster runs found two library defects. Each is filed and
quarantined in `known_bugs.yaml` on the platforms it affects, with a
time-box:

- **ROCM-32151**: some bf16 Stream-K solutions on gfx942 and gfx950
write about half the right value in the last partial M tile (rows 1024
to 1030 at M = 1031), and gfx950 solution 354888 does it in every row.
On gfx942 these solutions are offered only with
`TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2`, so the bf16 every-solution case
stays active there and fails only in that manual mode. `hipblaslt-bench
-v` pinned to each solution index fails the CPU reference; the
heuristic's default passes. The quarantine covers the whole bf16
configuration on gfx950; there is no way yet to exclude single
solutions.
- **ROCM-32153**: gfx950 f16 solutions 405799 and 407668 return wrong,
sometimes non-integer, values at 4099 x 2053 x 129. `hipblaslt-bench -v`
confirms 407668.

## Test Plan

- Host self-test: the solution log lists only failing solutions, with
their kernels and iterations, and is empty when everything passed.
- Device self-test: the corruption helper changes exactly one element,
and never to the value it held.
- `matmul_fast_check_repeat_reports_injected_iteration`, plus a mutation
check: corrupting iteration 3 instead of 2 must make the self-test fail
on both counts.
- All existing fast_check cases still pass with `fast_check_repeat` at
its default of 1.
- The Stream-K cases skip without the variable and run with it, and skip
on a GPU whose library offers no Stream-K kernel.

## Test Result

**ROCm 10.2, at the stack tip (3364b793ac1, which includes this PR).**
Every fast_check case and self-test passed or skipped for a stated
reason on gfx90a, gfx942 and gfx950, with none failing; the counts are
in #12876. With `TENSILE_SOLUTION_SELECTION_METHOD=2`:

- gfx942 (MI300X): 52 passed, 12 quarantined, and the 6 bf16
every-solution cases found ROCM-32151 again (all 32 failing solutions
are Stream-K kernels).
- gfx950 (MI350X): 43 passed and the other 28 are quarantined.
- gfx90a (MI210), which has no Stream-K library: all 40 Stream-K cases
now skip with "none of the N solutions for this case is a Stream-K
kernel", where before they passed while testing none.

Earlier development runs on gfx90a (MI210):

- Mutation check: with the wrong iteration corrupted, the self-test
failed for all 8 solutions with "the corrupted iteration 2 passed" and
"iteration 3 was not corrupted but failed".
- One run of the full filter crashed with a segmentation fault in a
`matmul_fast_check_matches_unit_check` case that also runs the host
reference; that case passed alone, its 64-case group passed, and later
full runs passed, so I could not reproduce it.
- gfx1250 was not run.

